%% DM26-0670

%% How the credentials agent's graph projection keeps up, as built (2026-11-04, credentials-agent/consume/src/projection.rs). The ledger is the record, and the graph can be rebuilt from it:
%% this never gates the agent's health or a reply. Each event is also projected as it happens (project_single_event), its checkpoint in the same transaction.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant GC as GraphControllerActor<br/>(the projection's child)
    participant Projection as ProjectionActor
    participant Ledger as LedgerActor
    participant Graph as Neo4j

    Note over GC,Projection: GraphSignal::Available fires at start, on every canary tick (30 s),<br/>and after every operation that sent something: not only on a reconnection
    GC--)Projection: GraphSignal::Available
    Projection->>GC: Query: MATCH (n:CredentialsProjectionCheckpoint) RETURN n.last_hash
    GC->>Graph: read
    Graph-->>GC: last_hash, or no row if nothing was ever projected
    GC-->>Projection: last_hash
    Projection->>Ledger: GetFullHistory
    Ledger->>Ledger: read the whole log from disk, every (hash, event) in order
    Ledger-->>Projection: the history
    Projection->>Projection: fold through a fresh state, event by event, so each has its historical context,<br/>and emit operations only after last_hash
    alt nothing new
        Note over Projection: Nothing to do. A last_hash not in the history also emits nothing, without a word
    else something new
        Projection-)GC: Op(Transaction { catch-up operations, the new checkpoint }), cast, with no reply
        GC->>Graph: atomic write
        alt it fails
            GC--)Projection: GraphSignal::OpFailed: logged, and tried again at the next Available, within 30 s
        else it succeeds
            GC--)Projection: GraphSignal::Available, which finds nothing new
        end
    end
